Ladybird integrates the pointer-derived scroll speed over each frame
interval, capped at 100ms. Gecko’s AutoScrollChild.autoscrollLoop
uses the animation frame timestamp and caps the interval at 100ms.
Blink’s AutoscrollController::HandleMouseMoveForMiddleClickAutoscroll
sends the velocity through ChromeClient::AutoscrollFling. WebKit’s
AutoscrollController::autoscrollTimerFired calls panScroll on the
renderer from a timer.

Chrome 158.0.8127.36, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 did not start
middle-button autoscroll in the headless macOS probes. The timing
comparisons for those engines come from their source. Ladybird’s two
frame intervals were measured with its rendering-opportunity test hook.
